<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6721"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 12:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->While reseching I found somthing that made me wonder! <BR> <BR>Shirley Vians maden name was Lawson. <BR> <BR>Now the the priciplal of the Adams Elementary School &#40;1002 N. Oliver&#41;  that Joseph  and Josephine Otero atended at the time of their murders, had the same name as Vians maiden name! <BR> <BR>What made me suspicious was what the pricipal stated in an interview :  &#34;Lawson recalled that even though the family had been in Wichita since November, a moving van had brought a load of furniture to the Otero home only about two days ago&#34; <BR> <BR>HOW would he know? was he there at their house watching? and if so WHY? <BR> <BR>Had he met/seen Julie Otero many times when she followed her children to school, was somthing about her tricking the &#34;monster&#34; in him?Was he facinated by little Josephine?  Here is the location of the AE school: <BR><a href="http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?zoomin=yes&amp;name=&amp;ed=lml4zOp_0TpDooKyylc6ilZMGX6jYJNcwwcyIJ15sC25dA76wQQBKdtRwqwVmxUB7VNFyUoDkbcU5h8KyPh88hS0WSfGI8qkqto7k5xyTALCRis-&amp;state=KS&amp;csz=Wichita%2C%2BKS%2B67208-2819&amp;ds=n&amp;uzip=67208&amp;mag=2&amp;desc=&amp;country=US&amp;dma=678&amp;cat=&amp;resize=l&amp;trf=0&amp;rezoom=0&amp;.intl=us&amp;compass=&amp;pan_x=0&amp;pan_y=0&amp;panable=1" target=_top>http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?zoomin=yes&amp;name= &amp;ed=lml4zOp_0TpD