<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6901"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 12:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->skov, this is very interesting. <BR> <BR>fwiw, take tina frederick&#39;s murder appears to have been &#34;officially solved&#34;- an individual, currently incarcerated for another murder, was charged with frederick&#39;s murder last august.  i just found this information yesterday at the <a href="http://members.fortunecity.com/ghostiesannex/wicoca.html">&#34;wichita cold cases&#34; page</a> maintained by another amautuer slueth. <BR> <BR>perhaps you can find other intersections with the principal or lawson family in the cold cases there or at my <a href="http://www.geocities.com/armchairpi/btk.htm">timline page</a>. <BR> <BR>i&#39;ve always found the children/school angle kind of interesting, but haven&#39;t persued it yet.  offhand, i&#39;m thinking anna williams and nancy fox are the only known victims without young children.  i wonder if they had connections to schools?  was it wegerle who even volunteered at a preschool?  this also brings up the whole &#34;pj&#39;s abc 123&#34; preschool issue again.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
